The '''2026 Vuelta a España''' was a three-week cycling race taking place in [[Monaco]], [[France]], [[Andorra]] and [[Spain]]. It started on 22 August in [[Monaco]] and finished on 13 September in [[Granada]].<ref name="route">{{cite web|title=Official route of La Vuelta 2026|url=https://www.lavuelta.es/en/overall-route|website=lavuelta.es|date=17 December 2025|access-date=23 December 2025}}</ref> It is the 81st edition of the [[Vuelta a España]] and the third and final [[Grand Tour (cycling)|grand tour]] of the [[2026 in men's road cycling|2026 men's road cycling season]].

The [[general classification in the Vuelta a España|general classification]] was won by [[Enric Mas]] of {{UCI team code|MOV|2026}}. Although [[Tadej Pogačar]] ({{UCI team code|UEX|2026}}) was widely expected to win the GC, and won three of the first six stages, he was injured in a crash on the eighth stage and forced to withdraw from the race. Mas, who was in second place when Pogačar crashed, inherited the red jersey, won the ninth stage, and defended his lead until the end of the Vuelta.

The [[points classification in the Vuelta a España|points classification]] was won by [[Wout van Aert]] ({{UCI team code|TVL|2026}}}, who also won two stages and the overall [[combativity award]]. Van Aert's teammate [[Matthew Brennan (cyclist)|Matthew Brennan]] won five stages, more than any other competitor. [[Santiago Buitrago]] ({{UCI team code|TBV|2026}}) won the [[mountains classification in the Vuelta a España|mountains classification]], and [[Oscar Onley]] ({{UCI team code|NCI|2026b}}), placing sixth in the overall GC standings, won the [[young rider classification in the Vuelta a España|young rider classification]].

== Teams ==
{{Main|List of teams and cyclists in the 2026 Vuelta a España}}
Twenty-three teams took part in the race. All eighteen [[UCI WorldTeam|UCI WorldTeams]] were automatically invited. They were joined by five [[UCI ProSeries|UCI ProTeams]]; the three highest ranked UCI ProTeams in 2025 ({{UCI team code|TUD|2026}}, {{UCI team code|PQT|2026}} and {{UCI team code|COF men|2026}}), along with two other Spanish teams ({{UCI team code|BBH|2026}} and {{UCI team code|EKP|2026}}). The teams were announced on 30 January 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=LA VUELTA 26: TEAM SELECTION - La Vuelta 2026 |url=https://www.lavuelta.es/en/news/2026/la-vuelta-26-team-selection/51093 |access-date=2026-02-08 |website=www.lavuelta.es |language=en}}</ref>
